<p>Curse you, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/croquembouche" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2893766); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2893766&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1602889320" alt="Croquembouche" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2893766)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/croquembouche" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2893766); return false;">Croquembouche</a></span>, for stealing the words from my mouth.</p>
<p>I don't think I have too much to say that Croq hasn't already said. The dialogue between Maliz and <em>anyone</em> absolutely shines, but at the end of the day they are right and this isn't an SCP. Simply posting it in a numbered slot does not make it so. And the attempt to jam it into an SCP format really hurts it - it leaves me with a lot of questions of &quot;why didn't the Foundation do X in response?&quot; Stuff like this:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A man in a white suit was spotted putting up identical leaflets in Boise's North End. Each leaflet bore anomalous text that cannot be perceived.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>gets left on the table. It's nothing major, but it ends up being a death by a thousand cuts situation.</p>
<p>But, that being said - I love the interplay between Maliz and the Man in White and Nobody too much. The Man in White playing off of Maliz's naivety that the Foundation has purpose and isn't fascist? Stroke of genius.</p>
<p>I'm gonna novote here.</p>

